Z||000000||varnster||11-12-2000||02:29 PM||||Im new to this site but I have gotten some<BR>good info so far. I cleaned the engine bay<BR>on my 87 fiero gt and got everything back together except the vacume lines for the cruise control,[didnt label them like an idiot] could some one help me out, I CANT FIND OUT WHERE THEY GO!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||11-12-2000||04:02 PM||||Well, I certainly <B>hope</B> you didn't label them like an idiot   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  If you need anything done like an idiot, I'm definitely qualified to help you   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>2 hoses go to the vacuum can: Larger-diameter hose goes from the aft fitting on the can, to an integral "T" in a metal line at the corner of the aft firewall. It "supplies" vacuum to the can.<P>Smaller-diameter hose goes from the other (forward) fitting on can, to lower fitting on diaphragm (the big actuator thingy w/throttle cable on it).<P>Another hose goes from upper fitting on the diaphragm, to a little vacuum solenoid on the aft firewall.   <P>Hope this helps.  <B>Now</B> you're cruisin'   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-12-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000002||varnster||11-12-2000||04:14 PM||||Thanks, I'll give it a try, next time<BR>I think I WILL TAKE THE TIME TO LABEL!||||reg||1
